# The generated kit — the placement models and the road surface textures — is tracked in Git LFS.
#
# It is regenerable (probes/editor-assets.mjs, probes/terrain-rockkit.mjs and
# pipelines/surfaces/gen.py) and too large for the plain object store, but the app image must ship
# it so a fresh editor draws the built-ins: the Dockerfile's `COPY apps/game/ apps/game/` puts
# `public/` into the build, which Vite copies into `dist/`. Git LFS keeps a clone small and the
# `worldeditor-image` job checks the blobs out with `lfs: true`.
apps/game/public/assets/*.glb filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
apps/game/public/surfaces/**/*.jpg filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
apps/game/public/surfaces/**/*.png filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
